## 2. Task Model

| **Name** | **Text** | **Relation** | **Location** | **Number of Robots** | **Justification** |
|----------|----------|--------------|--------------|----------------------|-------------------|
| **AT1** – *Navigate to Storage* | Move a robot from its current position to a specific storage location. | AND | *Storage* | `[1,n]` | Multiple robots may perform this navigation in parallel; `[1,n]` captures that flexibility. |
| **AT2** – *Send Resource Request* | Transmit a message to the storage with the exact resource specification. | AND | *Storage* | 1 | Only the robot that reached the storage sends the request. |
| **AT3** – *Wait for Retrieval* | Block until the storage confirms the resources are ready for pickup. | AND | *Storage* | 1 | The robot must wait for a confirmation before proceeding. |
| **AT4** – *Navigate to Delivery Location* | Move a robot from its current position to the delivery point. | AND | *Delivery Location* | `[1,n]` | Parallel deliveries can be executed by different robots. |
| **AT5** – *Deliver Resource* | Hand over the resource to the requesting agent. | AND | *Delivery Location* | 1 | Only the robot that has the resource performs the hand‑over. |
| **AT6** – *Return to Recharge Station* | Move a robot to the charging station for re‑charging. | AND | *Recharge Station* | 1 | Triggered when battery < 10 %. |
| **AT7** – *Return Resource to Checkpoint* | Move a robot carrying a resource to a safe checkpoint. | AND | *Checkpoint* | 1 | Triggered when battery < 30 %. |
| **AT8** – *Send Alert to Sector Manager* | Notify the sector manager of a failure to return the resource. | AND | *Sector Manager* | 1 | Only triggered on failure. |
| **AT9** – *Assign Mission to Another Robot* | Delegate the remaining collection or delivery tasks to an idle robot. | AND | *Base* | 1 | Only the robot that is re‑assigned performs this action. |
| **AT10** – *Return to Base* | Move a robot back to the base after completing a delivery run. | AND | *Base* | 1 | Standard end‑of‑run action. |
| **AT11** – *Assign Robots to Collection Tasks* | Allocate robots to specific storage locations based on current task list. | AND | *Base* | `[1,n]` | Parallel allocation can happen for multiple robots. |
| **AT12** – *Assign Robots to Delivery Tasks* | Allocate robots to specific delivery runs based on current task list. | AND | *Base* | `[1,n]` | Parallel allocation can happen for multiple robots. |

